<article class="env-lemma" id="0BNF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BNF">Lemma <span data-tag="0BNF">10.76.2</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $M = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits M_ i$ be a filtered colimit of $R$-modules. Let $N$ be an $R$-module. Then $\text{Tor}_ n^ R(M, N) = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits \text{Tor}_ n^ R(M_ i, N)$ for all $n$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a free resolution $F_\bullet $ of $N$. Then $F_\bullet \otimes _ R M = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits F_\bullet \otimes _ R M_ i$ as complexes by Lemma <a href="/tag/00DD" data-tag="00DD">10.12.9</a>. Thus the result by Lemma <a href="/tag/00DB" data-tag="00DB">10.8.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>